<title>FRANCE: Bull to raise 335.9 mln Ffr new capital.</title>
<headline>Bull to raise 335.9 mln Ffr new capital.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French computer maker Compagnie des Machines Bull will increase its capital by 335.9 million francs, not by 400 million as it had announced in December, a spokesman for Bull said on Monday.</p>
<p>The group expects to raise 218.9 million francs through the issue of shares and 117 million from the exercise of warrants by key shareholders France Telecom, NEC of Japan and Motorola, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>As a result of the operations, the state's stake in Bull will drop to 30.49 percent from 37 percent.</p>
<p>The stakes of France Telecom, NEC and Motorola will rise to 18.7 percent each from 17 percent, and Dai Nippon Printing's holding will rise to 5.8 percent from 3.33 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
